.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::MeshManager< dim >"Manages the creation, deletion, storage and connectivity of \fBElement\fP, \fBFace\fP and \fBInterFace\fP objects\&. 

Contains and updates \fBFiniteElementManager\fP, \fBFiniteVolumeStencilManager\fP, and \fBNodeManifoldManager\fP\&.

.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
nodes must be assigned to the elements as specified in CSMP_FEM_conventions\&.pdf following a right-hand coordinate system 

.PP
the elements must be compatible with one-another 

.PP
no hanging nodes 

.PP
no degenerate elements with collocated nodes, non-manifold vertices, triangle boxes etc\&. must be contained in the input mesh 

.PP
no interpenetrating elements
.RE
.PP
The connectivity that is maintained at all times consists of:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
cells (\fBElement\fP, \fBFace\fP, \fBInterFace\fP) are connected to their equidimensional neighbors; Elements to Elements, Faces to Faces etc\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
there is only one such neighbor per cell; potential manifolds that can arise for lower-dimensional cells are disambiguated by choosing the most closely aligned line segments or surfaces with the nearest normal orientation
.IP "\(bu" 2
nodes are connected to their neighbors except for NodeManifolds connecting collocated but topologically separated nodes
.IP "\(bu" 2
nodes know their parent \fBElement\fP objects (not Faces nor Interfaces)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBFace\fP objects are connected to their higher dimensional \fBElement\fP neighbors; if located on the outside of the model, their inner neighbor will be connected so that their normal points outside of the model
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBInterFace\fP objects can only occur on the inside of the model, being connected to two higher-dimensional \fBElement\fP neighbors
.PP

.PP
When the \fBMeshManager\fP creates or deletes cells, the connectivity in the surroundings is updated

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
MESHMANAGER IS AGNOSTIC ABOUT REGIONS, BOUNDARIES, AND SPLIT BOUNDARIES; it only handles creation, deletion and connectivity of cells and nodes!

.PP
Changes in the mesh affect \fBRegion\fP, \fBBoundary\fP and \fBSplitBoundary\fP objects meaning that they must updated, using corresponding functionality of ModelSubdomain and the Region-, Boundary- and \fBSplitBoundary\fP interfaces (policies) of \fBModel\fP\&. To support this, the \fBMeshManager\fP sets the supplied pointers to deleted items to NULLPOINTER\&. This way they can be deleted from the supplied cell ranges\&. If an object that should be deleted cannot, the pointer to it will not be nulled\&.

.PP
the pointers to items that shall be deleted from the colony are wrapped in iterators that allow setting the pointers to zero rather than just copies of them see method interfaces; For objects that are not going to be deleted, const-pointer access is granted\&.
.RE
