.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBvector\fP< \fBInterFace\fP< dim > * > \fBcsmp::MeshManager\fP< dim >::ReplaceElementsByInterFaces (const \fBPropertyDatabase\fP< dim > & , typename std::vector< \fBFaceConstructionData\fP< dim > >::iterator first, typename std::vector< \fBFaceConstructionData\fP< dim > >::iterator last, typename std::vector< \fBNode\fP< dim > * >::const_iterator perim_first, typename std::vector< \fBNode\fP< dim > * >::const_iterator perim_last, std::set< \fBNode\fP< dim > * > & split_perimeter_nodes, std::set< size_t > & region_material_ids, bool convert_original_elements_to_intervening_elements)"

.PP
replaces supplied \fBFace\fP objects with \fBInterFace\fP ones adding necessary nodes and node manifolds, establishing new connectivity; the input Faces are deleted Replaces supplied dim-1 \fBElement\fP objects with \fBInterFace\fP objects, adding the necessary multiplicated nodes, identifying outside elements and flagging regions for rebuild and establishing their connectivity\&. Since the \fBFace\fP objects are deleted the supplied pointer ranges to them (interior and perimeter) are invalidated by this method\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdbase\fP is needed for the inialisation of the \fBLocalVariableStorage\fP associated with the \fBFace\fP objects
.br
\fIfirst\fP iterator to the first \fBFaceConstructionData\fP of the supplied dim-1 region
.br
\fIlast\fP iterator to the last \fBFaceConstructionData\fP of the dim-1 region which also points behind the last perimeter face
.br
\fIperim_first\fP iterator to perimeter node vector of dim-1 region
.br
\fIperim_last\fP iterator to perimeter node vector of dim-1 region
.br
\fIregion_material_ids\fP for material identifiers placed on Elements, Regions etc\&.
.RE
.PP
A set which will be overwritten by method with region_identifier ids which should be scheduled for rebuilding since the elements (outside) have new nodes

.PP
@assumption Assumes element property "region identifier" is defined\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
: This method sets TOPO flags PERIMETER_LINE and PERIMETER_POINT
.RE
.PP
Steps - Creation of interfaces from \fBFaceConstructionData\fP:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
Loops over \fBFaceConstructionData\fP and duplicates nodes of InnerParent if they are found to Not be within the Perimeter Nodes supplied\&. If nodes are at a perimeter, no duplication occurs\&. If nodes are already a manifold (intersection), then duplication occurs (even at perimeter)\&.
.IP "2." 4
INTERNAL flags are added to nodes on both INSIDE and OUTSIDE unless at a model boundary\&.
.IP "3." 4
Outer Parent is assigned the new nodes created
.IP "4." 4
Interface objects are constructed based on Former higher-dimensional \fBElement\fP neighbors that are now connected to different nodes, but which share the same coordinates\&. Interface construction uses the coordinates to distinguish matching nodes\&. Higher dim elements unnassign each other as neighbors in the process\&.
.IP "5." 4
A neighbor search algorithm is performed on the outside of the interface objects which replaces the old inside node with the new duplicate node for all parent elements (perimeter nodes must be well defined for this to exclude the inside nodes from the assignment) All the outside elements are queried for their unique \fBRegion\fP they belong to using "region identifier" property, this is stored for \fBSplitBoundaryInterface\fP
.IP "6." 4
If a node on an existing interface was split (even if on perimeter), then the interface object is updated to contain (potentially) the duplicate node\&.
.IP "7." 4
Finally the node-to-parent element connectivity for the whole mesh is rebuilt\&.
.IP "8." 4
Likewise, the node-to-parent interface connectivity is also rebuilt, since all interfaces (new and old), now have correct nodes within them\&.
.PP

.PP
Cases: 3D: An X intersection, where the perimeter of split boundary 1 (not split), should be split in the dimension of splitboundary 2\&. Therefore, splitboundary node on INSIDE,OUTSIDE of SB1 is not split, and not manifold\&. However, same node, is classified a manifold by SB2, and is split, with different nodes on INSIDE OUTSIDE of SB2\&. How to disambiguate?

.PP
If split if manifold --> error when we split SB1\&.

.PP
